WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.127 --> 00:00:06.800
Speaker 1: This is also a bit of good news. The&nbsp;
Department of Justice is finally going to start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:15.200
a formal investigation into Donald Trump's 15&nbsp;
boxes of records that he had secreted away at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.320
Mar a Lago before they were turned over to the&nbsp;
National Archives, The Washington Post reporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:26.000
the Justice Department has begun taking steps&nbsp;
to launch an investigation into former President&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.080
Donald Trump's improper removal of presidential&nbsp;
records to Mar a Lago, some of which were labeled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.960
top secret. Remember, we couldn't vote for&nbsp;
Hillary, or we shouldn't because she couldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.440
be trusted with secret information. Trump's&nbsp;
flushing documents, incinerating documents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.680
eating documents, hiding, hiding away documents at&nbsp;
Mar a Lago. The people who spoke on the condition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.600
of anonymity to discuss an ongoing investigation&nbsp;
said the probe remained in the early stages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.160
It's not yet clear if the Justice Department&nbsp;
officials have started reviewing the materials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.040
in the boxes, or if they are seeking to interview&nbsp;
those who might have seen them or been involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:08.400
in assembling and moving them. The news comes&nbsp;
as the department faces increasing political&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.920
pressure to disclose its plans. On Thursday, House&nbsp;
Oversight Chairwoman Carolyn Maloney, Democrat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.960
from New York, accused the Justice Department&nbsp;
of obstructing her committee's investigation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:26.960
into the 15 boxes of records that Trump took with&nbsp;
him. So, number one, it's about time. Number two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.000
this is nothing other than step like zero point&nbsp;
one, but at least it's something and we'll see if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.880
and where it goes anywhere. And then again,&nbsp;
I mean, we I gave you some of these numbers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:45.440
during previous investigations into Trump with&nbsp;
Watergate. It was 783 days from the break in to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:53.280
Nixon's resignation. And even then, it was only&nbsp;
that quick because Nixon resigned. Here we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.320
a situation where Trump is no longer&nbsp;
president and we are only in the early stages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.800
It could be a very, very long time. Iran-Contra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:08.720
from Reagan announcing the investigation to&nbsp;
the end of the congressional investigation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.600
was two hundred and fifty four days. These things&nbsp;
do take a long time. I don't have high hopes. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.520
don't believe Trump is going to do a day in&nbsp;
prison. You guys already know. I think that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:24.640
But it does look that, you know, even in the best&nbsp;
cases where something provably wrong was done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:31.600
it still takes a really long time. Merrick Garland&nbsp;
got to get his act together. And as a reminder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.160
Joe Biden should have nothing to do with this&nbsp;
and he's not getting involved. That's the correct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.880
thing, as we spoke about yesterday. Joe Biden&nbsp;
should do nothing to encourage or interfere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.640
with an investigation into Hunter Biden. Joe Biden&nbsp;
should do nothing to interfere with or encourage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.840
an investigation into anything that Donald&nbsp;
Trump has done. But the Justice Department&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.280
is starting, and that's good news, and it will&nbsp;
likely mean more legal fees for Donald Trump.

